WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.263 --> 00:00:05.202
- Hello Believe Nation, my
name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:05.202 --> 00:00:07.181
My one word is believe.

00:00:07.181 --> 00:00:10.287
I believe in people more than
they believe in themselves.

00:00:10.287 --> 00:00:13.325
My sincere hope is that if you see in you

00:00:13.325 --> 00:00:17.279
what I see in you, you'll go
off and change the planet.

00:00:17.279 --> 00:00:20.202
I started the Believe Love series because

00:00:20.202 --> 00:00:21.898
having a relationship can be hard.

00:00:21.898 --> 00:00:23.331
And especially hard for entrepreneurs

00:00:23.331 --> 00:00:26.971
because we are managing
a child in our business

00:00:26.971 --> 00:00:28.951
and also a relationship.

00:00:28.951 --> 00:00:31.975
I thought it'd be of great value to myself

00:00:31.975 --> 00:00:34.663
and also to you guys to share some advice,

00:00:34.663 --> 00:00:37.301
some expertise and knowledge from people

00:00:37.301 --> 00:00:39.725
who are having successful
businesses and careers

00:00:39.725 --> 00:00:41.664
and also relationships and marriages

00:00:41.664 --> 00:00:44.049
and how to make it all work together.

00:00:44.049 --> 00:00:46.447
Today we're going to learn
from Jada and Will Smith

00:00:46.447 --> 00:00:49.390
and their message of don't quit.

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:50.963
- I know who's here with me tonight.

00:00:50.963 --> 00:00:52.513
- After 20 years, she knows your scent.

00:00:52.513 --> 00:00:54.807
- I know the touch, I know the scent,

00:00:54.807 --> 00:00:56.740
I know the energy, everything.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:58.156
- I told her, we were
just talking about that.

00:00:58.156 --> 00:00:59.741
I said, "That look of love that I saw

00:00:59.741 --> 00:01:02.485
"when you all walked onto
this carpet, my goodness."

00:01:02.485 --> 00:01:05.219
- You know, Jada, 'cause we've survived.

00:01:05.219 --> 00:01:07.077
- We have, we've survived.

00:01:07.077 --> 00:01:10.048
- That's the thing that is difficult

00:01:10.048 --> 00:01:11.697
that people don't understand about love.

00:01:11.697 --> 00:01:13.415
You think it's all flowers and everything

00:01:13.415 --> 00:01:17.082
but love gets created
by making it together.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:19.992
It's like it's from survival.

00:01:19.992 --> 00:01:21.281
- We've come through some stuff.

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:23.394
- This is a gangster right
here in front of you all.

00:01:23.394 --> 00:01:25.002
This little one here a gangster.

00:01:25.002 --> 00:01:26.070
(laughing)

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:27.214
Ride or die.

00:01:27.214 --> 00:01:30.546
- It can't be easy always
to make a relationship work.

00:01:30.546 --> 00:01:33.367
You talked about recently,

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:35.085
marriage being a hard thing to work on.

00:01:35.085 --> 00:01:36.531
What did you mean by that?

00:01:36.531 --> 00:01:40.698
- Everything that you do that's
great is going to be difficult.

00:01:44.507 --> 00:01:46.974
The most difficult part
about a relationship

00:01:46.974 --> 00:01:50.962
is that it's really not between two people

00:01:50.962 --> 00:01:51.795
that makes it work.

00:01:51.795 --> 00:01:53.878
It's between you and you.

00:01:56.047 --> 00:01:59.635
What Jada and I have learned
is bettering ourselves

00:01:59.635 --> 00:02:04.343
individually is how you
make a relationship work.

00:02:04.343 --> 00:02:06.520
If you're going to have counseling,

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:10.159
marriage counseling isn't
always the way to go.

00:02:10.159 --> 00:02:13.277
Individual counseling,
you get yourself together,

00:02:13.277 --> 00:02:15.802
and present yourself to your partner

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:18.374
in a higher spiritual and emotional state

00:02:18.374 --> 00:02:20.725
and you'd be surprised how
much better things can go.

00:02:20.725 --> 00:02:23.395
If there is a secret, I would say,

00:02:23.395 --> 00:02:28.346
is that we never went into
working on our relationship.

00:02:28.346 --> 00:02:31.342
We only ever worked on
ourselves individually

00:02:31.342 --> 00:02:33.629
and then presented
ourselves to one another

00:02:33.629 --> 00:02:35.783
better than we were previously.

00:02:35.783 --> 00:02:37.861
If you don't have a goal,

00:02:37.861 --> 00:02:40.984
if you don't have a purpose
for your relationship

00:02:40.984 --> 00:02:42.575
and pretty much anything.

00:02:42.575 --> 00:02:43.974
It's, like, if you don't have a purpose,

00:02:43.974 --> 00:02:46.365
if you don't have a
place that you're going,

00:02:46.365 --> 00:02:47.433
something that you want to accomplish,

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:48.954
something you want to do,

00:02:48.954 --> 00:02:52.123
you can really get lost in
the murk of the journey.

00:02:52.123 --> 00:02:53.371
- There has to be a vision for--

00:02:53.371 --> 00:02:54.765
- There has to be a vision, right.

00:02:54.765 --> 00:02:56.765
So, why are we together?

00:02:58.073 --> 00:03:01.156
I mean, you fine, you fine, you know.

00:03:02.189 --> 00:03:06.189
But as an answer for why two
spirits would join together

00:03:06.189 --> 00:03:09.294
and decide to travel this perilous journey

00:03:09.294 --> 00:03:11.433
of life together.

00:03:11.433 --> 00:03:14.408
Fine or you can cook or you
keep the house protected,

00:03:14.408 --> 00:03:15.906
that's really not enough.

00:03:15.906 --> 00:03:19.906
There's so much more that
you have to be dedicated to.

00:03:19.906 --> 00:03:23.621
- Will and I are very
relaxed with one another.

00:03:23.621 --> 00:03:27.812
I think because from how
I've answered questions of,

00:03:27.812 --> 00:03:31.887
"Girl, what would you do if he came home

00:03:31.887 --> 00:03:32.851
"and this and that and that."

00:03:32.851 --> 00:03:35.800
Or, "Being married to a
big superstar like Will,

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:37.106
"how do you deal with other women?"

00:03:37.106 --> 00:03:39.944
My answer's always,
"I've always told Will,

00:03:39.944 --> 00:03:40.861
"you can do

00:03:41.719 --> 00:03:43.219
"whatever you want

00:03:44.469 --> 00:03:48.636
"as long as you can look
at yourself in the mirror

00:03:49.556 --> 00:03:50.723
"and be okay."

00:03:52.824 --> 00:03:56.853
Because at the end of the
day, Will is his own man.

00:03:56.853 --> 00:04:01.149
I'm here as his partner
but he is his own man.

00:04:01.149 --> 00:04:04.765
He has to decide who he wants to be

00:04:04.765 --> 00:04:07.325
and that's not for me to do for him.

00:04:07.325 --> 00:04:08.504
Or vice versa.

00:04:08.504 --> 00:04:10.187
- I'm a hopeless romantic.

00:04:10.187 --> 00:04:13.142
I've made the distinction
between romance and love.

00:04:13.142 --> 00:04:16.725
Real love is born of
surviving with someone

00:04:18.401 --> 00:04:20.822
where you develop true love.

00:04:20.822 --> 00:04:24.670
- In that have a certain
understanding of what is needed.

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:27.926
I think that with marriages,
people have to understand

00:04:27.926 --> 00:04:30.725
that you have to look at your marriage

00:04:30.725 --> 00:04:34.893
and understand what is
needed in your marriage.

00:04:34.893 --> 00:04:37.633
Not what people think
your marriage should be.

00:04:37.633 --> 00:04:39.984
Not what people want your marriage to be.

00:04:39.984 --> 00:04:41.981
But I have to look at my husband

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:44.907
and I have to look at him
and look at what he needs

00:04:44.907 --> 00:04:46.329
as an individual.

00:04:46.329 --> 00:04:49.278
He has to look at me and see what I need.

00:04:49.278 --> 00:04:50.584
Then we have to look at the union

00:04:50.584 --> 00:04:52.093
and see what the union needs.

00:04:52.093 --> 00:04:54.915
We have to make decisions based on that.

00:04:54.915 --> 00:04:58.322
Not based on what people
think marriage should be.

00:04:58.322 --> 00:04:59.439
- I got to just ask out of personal,

00:04:59.439 --> 00:05:02.260
'cause you guys are such a cool couple,

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:04.860
another anniversary, was it, recently?

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:05.693
That is so cool.

00:05:05.693 --> 00:05:07.676
What advice, I got little kids,

00:05:07.676 --> 00:05:08.871
only been married a little bit,

00:05:08.871 --> 00:05:10.816
what advice could you pass
on to your boy right here?

00:05:10.816 --> 00:05:12.563
- Just stay in it.
- Just stay in it.

00:05:12.563 --> 00:05:13.864
- Just keep on trucking.

00:05:13.864 --> 00:05:15.684
(laughing)

00:05:15.684 --> 00:05:19.048
'Cause you got little kids
so I know what that's about.

00:05:19.048 --> 00:05:20.125
It gets real.
- It becomes about them

00:05:20.125 --> 00:05:23.271
but you can't forget
about you either, right?

00:05:23.271 --> 00:05:26.992
- Marriages go through many
different cycles and stages.

00:05:26.992 --> 00:05:29.413
It gets better and better and better.

00:05:29.413 --> 00:05:31.549
You will go through some tough patches,

00:05:31.549 --> 00:05:35.101
some really bad ones that are
going to make you want to quit,

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:37.937
going to make you want to quit, but don't.

00:05:37.937 --> 00:05:39.647
- She's about making
about to cry right now.

00:05:39.647 --> 00:05:40.957
(laughing) Okay.

00:05:40.957 --> 00:05:43.124
- And you want to kill,
makes you want to kill him.

00:05:43.124 --> 00:05:44.418
(laughing)

00:05:44.418 --> 00:05:45.547
- That is real talk.

00:05:45.547 --> 00:05:46.380
- I love it, real talk.

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:47.213
- Just stay in, just stay in.

00:05:47.213 --> 00:05:48.133
- All right, all right.

00:05:48.133 --> 00:05:49.844
I'm going to go pray about that tonight.

00:05:49.844 --> 00:05:52.474
- We've been married 20 years.

00:05:52.474 --> 00:05:55.807
We've been asking ourself that question.

00:05:56.758 --> 00:06:00.925
Really, at the end of the
day, it's just not quitting.

00:06:02.546 --> 00:06:05.129
You can't expect it to be easy.

00:06:06.156 --> 00:06:09.129
Our marriage was the
most difficult, grueling,

00:06:09.129 --> 00:06:12.275
and excruciating thing
that we've ever taken on

00:06:12.275 --> 00:06:13.358
